"""The port's own strings in the game's languages: writes recompwin/data/lang/<LANGUAGE>.txt (the format is in recomp/runtime/pclang.h).

A row is the English, then French, German, Italian, Spanish and Swedish. A row whose English starts with # is one of the game's own strings
by its LanguageID, which the port says differently (a save folder for the memory card, the PC's keys for the PS2's buttons); the rest are
the port's menus. \\xNN in a text is a byte as it is: the game's button icons are 0x80 to 0x8d. @ breaks a line.

A language of your own: copy one of the files, give it @name, and translate the right-hand side (see pclang.h for one the game does not have).
"""
